Package: zugojson
Title: JSON Formatting with a Parser Written in 'Goose'
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Wouter", "van Oortmerssen", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = paste("author of the 'Goose' language and compiler;",
                           "the JSON sample the parser derives from, the",
                           "runtime code the generated C inlines and the",
                           "runtime pieces in src/goose_vendor.c")))
Description: Formats, minifies and validates 'JSON' text with a parser and
    printer written in the 'Goose' programming language
    (<https://github.com/aardappel/goose>) and compiled ahead of time to C,
    which the package bundles. 'Goose' is a memory-safe systems language
    with no heap: the parsed document lives in one contiguous block linked
    by 4-byte relative offsets. The package replaces the 'Goose' runtime
    with a small one that reports every runtime failure as an R error
    instead of ending the process. No 'Goose' compiler is needed to install
    the package.
